# The guard who rides the crane lift (scene 0's object 8): his comportement
# at 642 is where the hero's script sends him when she talks to him (the
# original: he faces her and, in chapters 0-1, says "we're going to
# dissect... uh, I mean... take care of you!"). For Zoe he says nothing: he
# goes for her (his comportement 662, as when the office guard calls him),
# unless she's in the scientist's coat; then he carries on (561: back to the
# comportement his cube flags say). Written over the original's 20 bytes
# at 642 (zoe_prison.txt: patch 8 642).

== life
talk:                       # offset 642
  IF BODY_OBJ(0) != 4 else @carry_on
  SET_COMPORTEMENT 662
  END_COMPORTEMENT
carry_on:
  ELSE 561
